  "body": "podliner v2.2.1\n\nfixes for resuming episodes (#39) and for positions that got mixed up between episodes.\n\n## fixed\n\n- **streamed episodes did not resume where you left off.** podliner told the engine where to start only 350 ms after it began. by then a stream is usually still opening, so mpv threw the position away and the episode started at 0:00. the position now goes with the play itself, for every engine. thanks to dmaglio for the detailed report.\n- **vlc could hang at 0:00 when resuming.** it moved to the saved position from inside one of its own callbacks, which libvlc does not allow.\n- **a slow or broken stream wiped the saved position.** while an episode loaded podliner saved 0 as its position, so quitting before it started lost your place.\n- **switching episodes could carry the old position over.** right after a switch the new episode briefly took the position of the one before, which could mark a short episode as played.\n- **while a resumed episode loaded the list showed it as unplayed.** it now keeps showing where it resumes and \"loading…\" stays until it really plays.\n"
